Chapter: NothingAsValue

  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 'Nothing' is a type, not a value. Returning it where a Maybe is
 expected is the classic Haskell-to-Codex slip; the empty Maybe value
 is 'None'. CDX2086 names the fix instead of a generic unknown-name.

Section: Definitions

  find : Integer -> Maybe Integer
  find (x) = Nothing

  opening : Maybe Integer = find 3

